Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?dos:=20Phase=2012=20patch=200051=20=E2=80=94=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?SDL/0050=20shutdown=20bypass=20(fixes=20iter=20L=20L1=20freeze)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Iter L L1 (SDL/0050 default ON) delivered +8-13 fps in heavy gameplay
(30 fps milestone hit), BUT introduced a shutdown freeze on Quit-to-DOS
requiring operator reboot. L1.LOG ended after engine-side OPL3 close
("opl3 backend shutdown ..."), never reached "Sound system shutdown"
or "Renderer::Close()" lines that L2 (gate killswitched via
SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_QUIESCENCE_GATE=0) emitted cleanly.

Root cause: SDL/0050's GetDeviceBuf quiescence gate calls SDL_Delay(10)
inside the audio-thread iter while holding device->lock. When SDL audio
close path sets device->shutdown atomic + waits in SDL_WaitThread, the
audio thread's 10 ms SDL_Delay holds device->lock; if main thread also
needs the lock for SDL_CloseAudioDevice's internal cleanup, the
cooperative scheduler deadlocks before the atomic shutdown signal can
propagate through the gate's idle-cycle. Same class as the SDL/0046
WaitDevice deadlock fix — cooperative scheduler + paused audio path =
audio thread doesn't drain shutdown signal.

Fix: read device->shutdown atomic at top of DOSSOUNDBLASTER_GetDeviceBuf
BEFORE the quiescence walk + SDL_Delay throttle. If set, return the
staging buffer with *buffer_size unchanged (default-path return; normal
mix + PlayDevice). Audio thread does one final normal iteration;
PlaybackAudioThreadIterate's top-of-function shutdown check at
SDL_audio.c:1181 fires on the next iter; thread exits cleanly. Lock is
held only for the µs-class quiescence-walk-skip window, not the 10 ms
SDL_Delay window.

SDL_GetAtomicInt is lock-free (mirrors WaitDevice's pattern at
SDL_dosaudio_sb.c:437 added by SDL/0046). Safe to read here even with
device->lock held by PlaybackAudioThreadIterate.

Validation status:
- Gameplay smoke (DOSBox-X --fast): GREEN. Game launches, hits title,
  accepts input, no crash, 8 screenshots clean.
- Real-HW iter M validation needed: must observe "Sound system shutdown"
  + "Renderer::Close()" lines emit cleanly post-Quit (per L2's clean
  shutdown reference).

5-line meaningful change. No new env vars, no new public API. Coexists
with SDL/0050's killswitch — when killswitch=0 the quiescence walk is
skipped entirely (so the bypass never matters); when killswitch unset/
default-on the bypass fires only during shutdown.

Companion patches:
  SDL/0037 — idle-pause API + auto-engage IRQ-counter
  SDL/0038 — SB16 IRQ-5 instrumentation
  SDL/0040 — force-DSP-pause hint (fps measurement)
  SDL/0046 — WaitDevice shutdown bail (sibling deadlock fix)
  SDL/0048 — ForcePause auto-resume race fix
  SDL/0050 — DOS GetDeviceBuf quiescence gate (this patch fixes its
             shutdown-time interaction with cooperative scheduler)

Cross-reference: docs/PHASE12-PIXTONE-DECOUPLE-DESIGN.md Option A.

Per `dosbox_not_behavioral_proxy_for_io.md`: DOSBox-X smoke is
structural-only; gameplay smoke confirms structural correctness but
does not exercise graceful Quit-to-DOS shutdown. Real-HW iter M is the
data + behavioral gate.
---
 src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
index e41b4d79a..296c43253 100644
--- a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
+++ b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
@@ -825,6 +825,37 @@ static Uint8 *DOSSOUNDBLASTER_GetDeviceBuf(SDL_AudioDevice *device, int *buffer_
 {
     struct SDL_PrivateAudioData *hidden = device->hidden;
 
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 12 patch 0051): shutdown bypass for the
+       SDL/0050 quiescence gate. When SDL audio close path has set
+       device->shutdown atomic, skip the gate's quiescence walk + the
+       SDL_Delay(10) throttle so the audio thread can promptly drain its
+       iter cycle and exit on the next iteration's top-of-function
+       shutdown check at SDL_audio.c:1181.
+
+       Same class as SDL/0046's WaitDevice shutdown bail. Iter L L1.LOG
+       showed shutdown freeze on Quit-to-DOS — log ended after engine-side
+       OPL3 close, never reached "Sound system shutdown" or "Renderer::Close()"
+       lines that L2 (gate killswitched) emitted cleanly. Operator required
+       reboot. Root cause: audio thread held device->lock during the gate's
+       SDL_Delay(10) throttle while main thread waited in SDL_WaitThread;
+       cooperative scheduler deadlocked on lock contention before the
+       atomic shutdown propagated through the gate's idle-cycle.
+
+       Fix: read device->shutdown atomic at top of GetDeviceBuf BEFORE the
+       quiescence walk + delay; if set, fall through to the default-path
+       return (staging_buffer with *buffer_size unchanged). Audio thread
+       does one final normal-mix iteration; PlaybackAudioThreadIterate's
+       top-of-function shutdown check at line 1181 fires on the NEXT
+       iteration; thread exits cleanly. Lock is held only for the µs-class
+       quiescence-walk-skip window, not the 10 ms SDL_Delay window.
+
+       SDL_GetAtomicInt is lock-free (mirrors WaitDevice's pattern at
+       line ~437); safe to read here even with device->lock held by
+       PlaybackAudioThreadIterate. */
+    if (SDL_GetAtomicInt(&device->shutdown)) {
+        return hidden->staging_buffer;
+    }
+
     /* DOSKUTSU patch (Phase 11 patch 0050, Phase 12 Option A): GetDeviceBuf
        quiescence gate. Returns *buffer_size = 0 to signal "skip this audio-
        thread iteration" when no logical-device bound streams have data.
